    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Has a bit of a funky delivery, and from what I can see, I think he gets good extension and hides the ball well, which will help the fastball velo play up. \n His fastball velo was in the 92-95 range, touching 96 in his first Brewers and AA start\n Slider was a bit slower than I expected (a bit more sweeper-ish than a true slider), but it looked really good with a lot of movement. \n Changeup showed some really nice flashes, could be above average, though can be a little firm. Would be nice to see a little more of a velo drop from the FB.\n The curve appears to be a pretty solid fourth pitch, that I think will be usable at every level.\n Starting to mix cutter in more as a Brewer, which would really compliment his other pitches well.\n Command is really good. Rarely making mistakes, living on the edges of the zone and hitting spots.\n I like his profile a lot, and would put him as my highest pitching prospect in the system at this very moment. A guy I think should crack some Top 100's next year.",
